  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="24917cef-fcac-595b-9445-e1952a8506f2" activityNameId="11f5b413-c8b3-5a45-ac05-3b6c6358b6fa" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xx Jute stalks, from fibre production, irrigated system, at farm</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xx Jute stalks, from fibre production, irrigated system, at farm
Production of Jute delivers the co-products ' jute fibres, irrigated system, at farm' and 'jute stalks, from fibre production, irrigated system, at farm'. An allocation was carried out based on economical and mass criteria ;
UUID: 04cc8d0c-80b9-3320-8aa7-b725079ac431
The inventories include the mainly manual cultivation of Jute from conventional production standards. Included steps are soil cultivation, pestizides fertilisation (mineral fertilizer), harvest, loading for transport and extraction of the fibres after retting process. 
Location: Data from expert gremiums Indian Jute Insitute and experts assumptions. India is the most important producers of Jute fibres
Technology: Cultivation of Jute from conventional production standards
Time period: undefined
Production volume: The world production 2006 was 2’466’620 t Jute (1’415’700 t from India)
Sampling: Expert interviews, literature data and assumptions. 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_04cc8d0c-80b9-3320-8aa7-b725079ac431.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="54f55fae-bf70-52c2-b2bc-7b92fd55ae8e" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
